1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,096
Contrastive Voice compares a recording

2
00:00:02,156 --> 00:00:05,544
with a reference reading of the same
words.

3
00:00:05,604 --> 00:00:09,424
It shows where the delivery departs, by
how much,

4
00:00:09,484 --> 00:00:12,873
and what that costs in a
reference-relative score.

5
00:00:12,933 --> 00:00:19,340
I will show the dataset, the stress tests,
and the dashboard with a live analysis.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,045
The reference recordings are public
domain: nine

7
00:00:23,105 --> 00:00:26,595
United States government speeches and ten
LibriVox readings.

8
00:00:26,655 --> 00:00:29,256
The source manifest records each download

9
00:00:29,316 --> 00:00:32,362
address, checksum, licence basis and
speaker split.

10
00:00:32,422 --> 00:00:37,242
The build selects one passage of about
thirty seconds from each

11
00:00:37,302 --> 00:00:41,235
speech by matching recognised words to the
official transcript.

12
00:00:41,295 --> 00:00:44,340
That favours passages the aligner handles
well.

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,151
The dataset is built in one Kaggle script
kernel on two T4 graphics processors.

14
00:00:51,211 --> 00:00:54,256
The runner checks the staged source
hashes,

15
00:00:54,316 --> 00:00:57,362
installs the locked environment, and runs
four

16
00:00:57,422 --> 00:01:00,024
stages: dataset, calibration, evaluation
and gallery.

17
00:01:00,084 --> 00:01:05,347
The final run took six hundred and
fifty-three seconds, about eleven minutes.

18
00:01:05,407 --> 00:01:09,340
The status file shows four of four stages
complete.

19
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,696
The dataset holds one hundred and

20
00:01:12,756 --> 00:01:15,912
twenty-one audio files, fifty-four point
one minutes.

21
00:01:15,972 --> 00:01:22,343
Nine speakers are split five for training,
two for validation and two for test.

22
00:01:22,403 --> 00:01:26,018
One hundred and two clips are generated:
identity

23
00:01:26,078 --> 00:01:29,234
controls, single-level clips, a ladder
from one

24
00:01:29,294 --> 00:01:33,828
small edit to a botched passage, and
edited second readers.

25
00:01:33,888 --> 00:01:39,340
Each label stores the edit type, level,
word span and sample span.

26
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,428
These flaws are controlled acoustic edits,
not

27
00:01:43,488 --> 00:01:48,411
human errors, and nobody has listened to
and rated them.

28
00:01:48,471 --> 00:01:53,394
There are eight edit types at three
levels: faster or

29
00:01:53,454 --> 00:01:56,882
slower speech, dropped or inserted pauses,
flattened

30
00:01:56,942 --> 00:02:00,869
pitch, removed emphasis, a fade, and
spectral smoothing.

31
00:02:00,929 --> 00:02:05,354
On the page, black bars mark the injected
edits,

32
00:02:05,414 --> 00:02:09,340
and shaded regions mark what the detector
flagged.

33
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,846
The examples form a spectrum of quality.

34
00:02:12,906 --> 00:02:15,337
Identity runs every recipe with neutral

35
00:02:15,397 --> 00:02:18,658
settings and scores one hundred with no
flags.

36
00:02:18,718 --> 00:02:24,055
From level one to level three the score
falls from ninety-seven to eighty-five.

37
00:02:24,115 --> 00:02:29,037
G five is the botched end: the whole
passage is rushed and

38
00:02:29,097 --> 00:02:34,019
flattened, with dropped pauses and fades,
and it scores forty point two.

39
00:02:34,079 --> 00:02:37,340
Listen to G five, then to the reference.

40
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,312
The test split has two speakers and was

41
00:02:53,372 --> 00:02:56,263
evaluated once, after the design was
frozen.

42
00:02:56,323 --> 00:02:59,635
Of thirty-two edits at levels two and
three,

43
00:02:59,695 --> 00:03:04,272
twenty-nine are matched one to one with at
least half overlap.

44
00:03:04,332 --> 00:03:07,223
With five false flags and three misses,

45
00:03:07,283 --> 00:03:11,438
strict event F one is zero point eight
seven nine.

46
00:03:11,498 --> 00:03:17,340
Matched region boundaries miss the label
by up to zero point nine eight seconds.

47
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,292
The stress matrix changes only the
recording channel.

48
00:03:21,352 --> 00:03:27,578
On the test recordings, a six decibel gain
change and MP3 coding add no regions.

49
00:03:27,638 --> 00:03:30,511
White noise at twenty decibels
signal-to-noise ratio

50
00:03:30,571 --> 00:03:34,702
adds one pace flag, and a low-pass filter
adds two.

51
00:03:34,762 --> 00:03:38,892
Heavy compression, about ten decibels of
gain reduction, is the

52
00:03:38,952 --> 00:03:44,340
failure: it adds five false pause and
volume flags in about one minute.

53
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:49,916
On edited test clips, twenty-nine edits
are found before

54
00:03:49,976 --> 00:03:54,340
stress, twenty-seven after noise, and
twenty-four after compression.

55
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:01,473
This is level three, set A, compared with
the recording it was edited from.

56
00:04:01,533 --> 00:04:06,607
The delivery score is eighty-five point
one, with six flagged regions.

57
00:04:06,667 --> 00:04:08,007
I select Rushed.

58
00:04:08,067 --> 00:04:12,673
The explanation names the words, gives the
span in both

59
00:04:12,733 --> 00:04:16,873
recordings, and says the speech took zero
point eight

60
00:04:16,933 --> 00:04:21,540
seven seconds against one point six two in
the reference.

61
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:24,340
It costs four point one points.

62
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,578
Button A plays this span in the
participant recording.

63
00:04:28,638 --> 00:04:32,215
Button B plays the same words in the
reference.

64
00:04:32,275 --> 00:04:38,278
The black bar is the injected edit, and
the shaded box is the flagged region.

65
00:04:38,338 --> 00:04:41,107
The category cards filter the list, and

66
00:04:41,167 --> 00:04:44,340
clicking a word in the transcript plays
it.

67
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,573
Now a different speaker.

68
00:04:56,633 --> 00:05:01,882
John Greenman reads the same passage, with
an inserted pause and a fade.

69
00:05:01,942 --> 00:05:07,190
The regime is R two, and its thresholds
are wide because two good

70
00:05:07,250 --> 00:05:11,273
readers differ a lot: twenty-two point
eight decibels for volume.

71
00:05:11,333 --> 00:05:15,357
Nothing is flagged and the score stays at
